From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StellarSeal <emnoigi1452@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:51:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 070/124] Skip BlockPhysicsEvent work when no listeners are
 registered

- Hoist a BlockPhysicsEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0 check into World neighborChanged so the event, its CraftBlock snapshot and the dispatch are skipped entirely when no plugin listens (backport of Leaf MC 0256; BlockPhysicsEvent can fire 50k+/sec during redstone, liquid and sand activity)
- Return null early from CraftEventFactory.callBlockPhysicsEvent when the handler list is empty and null-guard the BlockPlant and BlockTallPlant callers
- Add EventShortCircuitTest pinning the HandlerList and SimplePluginManager semantics the hoist relies on: fresh lists report zero listeners, zero-listener dispatch never cancels, and register/unregister flips the check live with no staleness

diff --git a/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPlant.java b/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPlant.java
index 16c8156..6f30323 100644
--- a/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPlant.java
+++ b/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPlant.java
@@ -41,7 +41,8 @@ public class BlockPlant extends Block {
     protected void e(World world, BlockPosition blockposition, IBlockData iblockdata) {
         if (!this.f(world, blockposition, iblockdata)) {
             // CraftBukkit start
-            if (org.bukkit.craftbukkit.event.CraftEventFactory.callBlockPhysicsEvent(world, blockposition).isCancelled()) {
+            org.bukkit.event.block.BlockPhysicsEvent event = org.bukkit.craftbukkit.event.CraftEventFactory.callBlockPhysicsEvent(world, blockposition); // Leaf - null when no listeners (backport of Leaf MC 0256)
+            if (event != null && event.isCancelled()) {
                 return;
             }
             // CraftBukkit end
